A||||4||maryjane||Non-Fiero pwr steering repair||||1||
Z||000000||maryjane||11-04-2001||05:28 PM||||I've got an old Jeep Cherokee, fishing & work vehicle, that leaks pwr steering fluid at the gear seal, not the pump. It's at the input, that is, where the steering column shaft connects to the gear assy. I think it is a Saginaw unit but not sure. I put one on it from a salvage yard, but it started leaking too, after about 90 days. There seems to be no slack or wear in the input shaft, so I guess the seal is just gone. Any body have any luck replacing the seal in one of these things?<BR>I'm using dextron III for pwr steering fluid. Is this the cause of my oily driveway?<BR>Thanks<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||11-04-2001||09:00 PM||||Anybody? A new one is gonna cost me about $200, I'm trying to spend a dollar or two less <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||11-04-2001||09:29 PM||||ATF is acceptable for topping off a power steering, but not for a total refill. You might try some of that Prestone leak stopper P/S fluid and see if it helps.||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||11-04-2001||09:33 PM||||Thanks, Cooter, I'll give it a try, but methinks it's past any of that type stuff. It will all leak out in about 4 days, either driving or sitting. Guess I better get the checkbook out--again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||PBJ||11-06-2001||09:48 PM||||Sounds like you are talking about the stub shaft and its seal. I have replaced a few before. Found in all cases a bit more work but less hassle to remove the gear box from the truck to do it.  Now all I know is GM but likely since it is a Jeep it is the same.  If you are unsure, remove the gear box and take it down to your dealer and have them bang a new seal in.<P>This is how I would do it.  <P>remove the gear box.<BR>scribe large outer ring (nut) and spin it off.<BR>scribe inner nut and spin it off and count turns (be exact)<BR>now seal will be accessible, be sure to clean any rust from stub shaft and lubricate seal.<P>I hope this helps.<P>Pete<BR>||||reg||1
